            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for one's home town, then the Mandarin for to relax."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: hǎojiǔ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hǎojiǔ — \"a long time; ages\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒmen hǎojiǔ méi jiànmiàn le — We haven't seen each other for ages."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones: hǎojiǔ is said háojiǔ, the first rising."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hǎojiǔ is built from 好 'good', here 'very', and jiǔ 'long-lasting', both inherited from Middle Chinese, xawX and kjuwX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'lasting long'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for times of day."
